  "notes": "Composed of {検|けん} (examine, inspect) + {死|し} (death). Strictly speaking, {検死|けんし} refers to the external examination of a body (also written {検視|けんし}), while {解剖|かいぼう} or {司法解剖|しほうかいぼう} refers to the internal autopsy. However, in common usage {検死|けんし} often covers both. Common collocations: {検死|けんし}を{行|おこな}う (to conduct a postmortem), {検死|けんし}{報告書|ほうこくしょ} (autopsy report), {検死|けんし}{官|かん} (coroner/medical examiner). Not to be confused with the homophone {剣士|けんし} (swordsman). Frequently appears in mystery novels and crime dramas.",
  "schema_version": "2.0",
